#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166586 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/id #uuid "7da1ada0-43e5-5807-b2c2-2a254a76cf27" :question/math-academy-id "e-8257" :question/problem "If $f(x,y) = 2\\sqrt{x+y}$ and $y=\\cos x,$ compute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y = y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+y}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526461 :question-generator/id #uuid "786f911d-355f-5878-9cda-bf6174bb6545" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186166748.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00add8e7-6980-56f0-9a2a-bb552536c12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357760} {:answer/id #uuid "286d61f8-a3ff-5fbf-b774-2c2cb79b67bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358115} {:answer/id #uuid "6d859cb3-66c2-535d-8f19-f1b8830867ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358708} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe84aab-93e0-5d36-b349-3a91b328cae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359385} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a2ec28-c873-5c71-8848-26eba34233c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbe84aab-93e0-5d36-b349-3a91b328cae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359385} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aac33cc-3f0e-5b51-8653-40c739dd5910" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78ec1810-6288-5fe9-a1ed-f6d4d3a585e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94588" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+y)$ and $y={x}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{x}^{2})=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{x}^{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e272a6d-78d3-5cb9-95c9-c87f0fea3da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357869} {:answer/id #uuid "34692782-e7a3-51e2-939e-c7595c3e9b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358219} {:answer/id #uuid "69e98fd7-fe36-540b-bd06-de9d5d7bdda7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})-\\frac{1+3{x}^{2}}{1+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358677} {:answer/id #uuid "7b57f18a-b391-5d2a-a9af-d8d06a8a7f7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)-\\frac{1+2{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358823} {:answer/id #uuid "9695921f-e190-55c7-a45b-cceb0f8f0066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e272a6d-78d3-5cb9-95c9-c87f0fea3da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357869} :answer-field/id #uuid "000855cc-b4eb-5315-a2d3-71276d48abd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56630566-56de-5b10-a1f2-1989c1203d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-95121" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$ and $y={x}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x+2{x}^{2}}{x+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x(1+2x)}{x(1+x)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021a846a-8825-55bf-a7b3-1dc5c5c5ff19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281709} {:answer/id #uuid "49b2d0a3-8640-5928-a7d2-f8a14102a68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282314} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a1e1c7-9e8a-5f17-9500-4d7507d44b3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283715} {:answer/id #uuid "efd819c9-60d2-5826-9266-3dba4a49aaec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283779} {:answer/id #uuid "f5de75cd-c44e-5baf-9f07-d98f3333edab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49b2d0a3-8640-5928-a7d2-f8a14102a68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282314} :answer-field/id #uuid "d658fcd0-7d37-5a87-a5b6-42706ffef583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdba7da9-8893-51f6-a38d-eccc847b176c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170670" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ and $y={x}^{2}+1,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{{x}^{2}+1}=2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134e5ec5-1833-5763-a152-935445c16e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357915} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfec4cb-8120-5f44-9db6-9fe99f5be666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357993} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd7195e-4163-5d9b-ab1f-f50c56f9bda4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358725} {:answer/id #uuid "a03e6cf2-e199-53c6-82f6-4585f233d777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359150} {:answer/id #uuid "e14a9608-4f8c-580c-b913-718d374bebe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a03e6cf2-e199-53c6-82f6-4585f233d777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359150} :answer-field/id #uuid "69e0f45c-fd3c-57d2-96aa-73479d2efe99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d95d5a8a-ad5f-52dc-beb9-600c878518d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95088" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+y}$ and $y={e}^{-x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}+\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f7371e6-fa62-5258-b977-84ee4e88782e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358438} {:answer/id #uuid "67710e58-3007-513b-8494-0c76521975c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358654} {:answer/id #uuid "80e19a52-081f-5b37-8339-414407ee7d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358876} {:answer/id #uuid "901dd65d-6c65-58cd-87bb-517a683c4833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359008} {:answer/id #uuid "96f6c6ee-cd4d-5972-a765-20abbc025c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96f6c6ee-cd4d-5972-a765-20abbc025c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d31946ed-c60d-5761-b68f-54a6782e1347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e7ed0c3-433c-5b76-94b3-8ee539ba166f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95114" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13df3da6-fa03-593a-b697-020ee592a4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357924} {:answer/id #uuid "205aa05e-a7f6-5abf-9311-2b838c211938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358036} {:answer/id #uuid "682e2303-0eea-58c6-9296-93c2403f441a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(1+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358663} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e70a37-4f39-508f-a9c2-c0d746a9d541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(1+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359443} {:answer/id #uuid "fa934368-527c-591b-bae3-d56a4c98c73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}(1-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "682e2303-0eea-58c6-9296-93c2403f441a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(1+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358663} :answer-field/id #uuid "97ecada2-93d5-5ee3-a2ef-d0b7948dd606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25aad332-4985-5005-bb5a-87ea911c6d16" :question/math-academy-id "q-95117" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(1+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be18679-efe0-59e6-80ac-db92f8d96a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358407} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9edd72-2523-57c6-9665-681f1ed475c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358439} {:answer/id #uuid "9bcdf56c-f98e-5632-8b37-69db930425d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359116} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b3c97-4572-526c-8afd-d0a1d5757af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359141} {:answer/id #uuid "b33efd16-e5a4-5396-8988-6df4afae8ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4be18679-efe0-59e6-80ac-db92f8d96a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358407} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f643ac2-8342-50cb-9136-e026a1d69059" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfb1f74a-0323-5d9e-a2f6-877356ed98f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-95118" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+yx$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dbcf33-c576-54cf-8c07-43b62cf69983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+4{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358069} {:answer/id #uuid "558df00d-6a5e-5bb3-bb8a-e8288e5b1e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1-4{x}^{3}}{x})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{{x}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358497} {:answer/id #uuid "67861fb7-92d5-5f5e-8f74-f8ff3c7f315c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-3{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358655} {:answer/id #uuid "70539894-ff4f-5b7d-809c-ae8c476c88fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1-2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358729} {:answer/id #uuid "da024232-5563-5f22-a044-1622a067232a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{x})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70539894-ff4f-5b7d-809c-ae8c476c88fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1-2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358729} :answer-field/id #uuid "f550e8b8-0dda-5ff3-ba5c-bfed41503899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f396a56-19fc-58e7-855c-d3a310fbb9ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-95119" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+y)$ and $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+y),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x})+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}))\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1-2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}+1}{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a85a62-20c8-53ea-9891-50994f57bf9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}(x-6)}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357811} {:answer/id #uuid "31bd0322-e103-58db-ab4e-d490d4079dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-1)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358194} {:answer/id #uuid "870209e6-e356-5edd-a169-1a95385cbde9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x(3x+4)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358933} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ec2678-1f3d-53f9-9edd-d1c6fda28115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x(4x-3)}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359444} {:answer/id #uuid "d1925cff-23b1-5f65-a480-35f2ce80acbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1925cff-23b1-5f65-a480-35f2ce80acbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359584} :answer-field/id #uuid "a27a35b5-3297-5a09-b127-d1d744a50e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f411889e-b3c1-5aed-8247-b760065e6e98" :question/math-academy-id "q-95122" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x+1}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{y}{(x+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{x+1}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}(x+1)-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125ca586-3337-5120-876d-92e40e11dbf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437260} {:answer/id #uuid "ba33cf18-d667-5a40-9d16-6cf17e9bc306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437263} {:answer/id #uuid "dacbed10-7956-5d58-b766-2a05b8deb073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437266} {:answer/id #uuid "dacc660c-f7e4-5ae5-93dd-d34894e5734f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437267} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c3c8e0-fd65-53d1-b833-3d4e2653e49b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1c3c8e0-fd65-53d1-b833-3d4e2653e49b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437269} :answer-field/id #uuid "f729b4c9-529c-5fb2-a0e6-3a129de28dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab9cce6f-4b79-504d-bebd-6e1b2e2dc75d" :question/math-academy-id "q-170671" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=(1-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=(1-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(1-{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e4af3f-61bc-5126-83bf-edde59b61b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478611} {:answer/id #uuid "3240fcea-f2a6-504a-8d73-e1a71cf1a1f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478635} {:answer/id #uuid "7dae59e3-fbbc-543f-9d25-16ccca4d11a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478747} {:answer/id #uuid "acf73fac-21b4-5b22-a6ba-f45bb952aa13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478842} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e3aeda-9359-5ed2-b5a4-5bdf7646a57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21e4af3f-61bc-5126-83bf-edde59b61b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478611} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f7da20-bbae-51ed-a0e8-82abd9017a31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "192e8101-5b84-55a9-943c-4057db856b4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95123" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{xy-4}$ and $y={x}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy-4}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy-4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{x\\cdot {x}^{2}-4}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{x\\cdot {x}^{2}-4}}=\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}+\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d5ecadd-1d99-51f3-b3ee-0d0a52a7e504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478669} {:answer/id #uuid "7eececa3-aed5-56bc-8acd-83a7d9f52ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+2{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478748} {:answer/id #uuid "c04864f4-8e0e-5d9d-8763-0a9d20cfc1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478870} {:answer/id #uuid "c22286df-0bd2-569b-80cb-dd78460f6e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478871} {:answer/id #uuid "fd87021b-423b-576b-b08a-47b84980a27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd87021b-423b-576b-b08a-47b84980a27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478956} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1b30ab-e87a-541b-926a-088f06d1391d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "889d0bfa-8294-56c7-a3ce-0b0d572aff69" :question/math-academy-id "q-95120" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$ and $y={e}^{2x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x+y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x+{e}^{2x}}+\\frac{1}{x+{e}^{2x}}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+{e}^{2x}}+\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2{e}^{2x}}{x+{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28030418-5f24-5272-86ce-e3723aabb231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526399} {:answer/id #uuid "58bcd153-e4a6-5347-b974-b9ed5dc0fe90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526414} {:answer/id #uuid "628cb4c0-5057-556d-a14c-1a38c916f6bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526416} {:answer/id #uuid "837ec4f1-2785-5592-84e2-6ce366787415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526425} {:answer/id #uuid "d1406d71-acc3-535d-9583-aa1c7ab89832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1406d71-acc3-535d-9583-aa1c7ab89832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526451} :answer-field/id #uuid "02eb60d5-5312-5ccf-8a81-9bea45dbebe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e7676fd-d001-5de3-b465-0aeb6e24740a" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + x y$ and $y=- \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f719175-0350-5ab1-8b31-b6444a8164e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526411} {:answer/id #uuid "564ef5c0-2148-5813-bea6-ba25040c8f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526413} {:answer/id #uuid "5df99349-f91f-5ae1-99b2-bcd6b3fc1586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526415} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0cd494-6b02-58ed-8cc8-2b861c96e086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526420} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8b0928-aa99-59cc-92d0-19375c21d27c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5df99349-f91f-5ae1-99b2-bcd6b3fc1586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526415} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f324d52-4c30-5c1d-bb2a-4a9f0a9dcf71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72cc3095-5d1d-534f-8f85-48cfe2429d46" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} - 2 x y$ and $y=- \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x - 2 y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =4 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\\\  & =2 \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1252db4f-6351-5996-b74d-6d5bf42f331e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526395} {:answer/id #uuid "2a485976-4f67-547b-b3d2-f48f0f3d4189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526401} {:answer/id #uuid "7f6fd225-cc83-5dab-bacf-849050e741c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526424} {:answer/id #uuid "88241d4f-b699-51c6-a094-8e175af83201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526428} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd3c03e-062b-5987-afd5-25a75a4ff6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccd3c03e-062b-5987-afd5-25a75a4ff6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526450} :answer-field/id #uuid "54c6b567-0bd7-5bb7-9bc9-1e721afcf635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d1cf1af-73f0-5835-a9c0-2ae46945e41a" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + x y$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=8 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8d57-eed3-5f7f-803c-e4b08b5a2fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526394} {:answer/id #uuid "487c1d4a-c93e-5489-bccb-93e33859361b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526408} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8680f2-cbde-55a5-95b1-4d2e08e21b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526409} {:answer/id #uuid "7387c28f-4867-5085-b7c6-81bc1baa6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526418} {:answer/id #uuid "e99a6ce9-68cd-5ec0-ab4c-c9f8479a2750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a8680f2-cbde-55a5-95b1-4d2e08e21b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526409} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd71c7d-3950-511e-bbd6-2df993c0ae98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f57aa56-b41b-566d-8ea7-a684dfb21253" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 x e^{- 3 y}$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=2 e^{- 3 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 6 x e^{- 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 6 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 24 x e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =- 2 \\left(12 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 1\\right) e^{- 3 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424393bd-012e-5487-b5fa-2d9b39260b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526407} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b23c9a-7d39-54a4-a0c2-ebe6cb589e5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526435} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cf6f21-2a5f-5fbe-af69-59ade2a54030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526436} {:answer/id #uuid "af678b84-5edb-5546-b998-af5d8656b803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x^{2} e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526439} {:answer/id #uuid "d4672b92-b3c7-54b8-80c8-31f3d94077aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4672b92-b3c7-54b8-80c8-31f3d94077aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 x \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526452} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1fc4e7e-ffc1-5cf5-8a0e-e7ccfe76dda1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "84520ae9-d161-55be-8813-c4f436891538" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 x e^{- 3 y}$ and $y=x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=2 e^{- 3 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 6 x e^{- 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1x) & =1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}) & =- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =24 x^{2} e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 6 x e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2 e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =2 \\left(12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right) e^{- 3 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186bfece-020c-5fef-8ded-f89e7e7c948a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x^{2} \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526397} {:answer/id #uuid "2936b0cb-ae36-59c0-b3e1-1f34022918b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526400} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9e9f8a-10b2-597f-898d-54d7713ef86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526402} {:answer/id #uuid "419ef840-0342-58fd-96ed-e9251fe88f29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526406} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5d9c50-a79b-57ab-af34-2bdd942f4a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "419ef840-0342-58fd-96ed-e9251fe88f29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) - x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526406} :answer-field/id #uuid "a06eaab3-3b05-5df8-b761-4fca2b88c718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "944dba1d-61e2-5ad6-8d02-a9d420bedc5f" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} + x y$ and $y=- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-1x) & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}) & =4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\cdot \\left(\\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(-1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 4 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 4 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} - 2 x \\\\  & =- 2 x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3efe972a-ae63-59cc-951a-d997c172f209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526405} {:answer/id #uuid "9006440e-db82-5fc3-92bd-e5850a7af94a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526429} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ac2c17-640c-56ec-95fe-b8e50c3da1a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526443} {:answer/id #uuid "c6304f6c-200a-5d54-a3ab-2464a638cbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526447} {:answer/id #uuid "d9089dac-faa8-52e2-a142-f4b5f18235ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 9 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6304f6c-200a-5d54-a3ab-2464a638cbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526447} :answer-field/id #uuid "77cd0f71-ea5d-5c78-95b1-fbad042b2a64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b4c83e15-bbb6-5da7-a44a-f955570eaf00" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + x y$ and $y=x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=8 x + y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1x) & =1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}) & =2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x+\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =2 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 8 x \\\\  & =2 x \\left(x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 4\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d6c0ef-cfa7-58c2-be53-de5a0505e20e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 x \\left(- 3 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526391} {:answer/id #uuid "161a5743-5095-522e-afc1-c1d35037ede5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526396} {:answer/id #uuid "350521a2-3cd2-51f6-8186-910915f4868f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526404} {:answer/id #uuid "a414ea7c-4694-569e-8c17-21e5b5cd9607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x^{2} e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526434} {:answer/id #uuid "c43f8d9c-d89a-5466-8bc8-2952bb1353bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x \\left(- 3 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c43f8d9c-d89a-5466-8bc8-2952bb1353bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x \\left(- 3 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526446} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5db5ae8-804c-5987-a194-276c13632d92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b643f6b7-d3f2-56a2-a67e-4927f1102909" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- 3 x e^{4 y}$ and $y=x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 3 e^{4 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 12 x e^{4 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 12 x e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1x) & =1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}) & =- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 3 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 12 x e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 3 x \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =36 x^{2} e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 12 x e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =3 \\left(12 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 1\\right) e^{4 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069f595e-b35c-55a4-ad9b-702391c1dbec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\left(- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526393} {:answer/id #uuid "91e115d3-8fbf-5c9d-9030-7416dc59ca16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\left(- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526430} {:answer/id #uuid "b14846b1-3e0e-5a3e-ba05-71414b61ce8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526440} {:answer/id #uuid "f86a2b1a-a2c9-52b8-bcff-859b18c41cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 4 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526459} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd5f0b4-0b9e-5bf3-ac26-08f99ebb67fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069f595e-b35c-55a4-ad9b-702391c1dbec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\left(- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) + 2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526393} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5bce036-a6e5-5c8c-a473-2756b116720c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8295975-e0c2-5952-8fb4-2cd0c1975736" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x^{2} - 2 x y$ and $y=- x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 2 x - 2 y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-1x) & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}) & =2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\cdot \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)+\\left(-1x\\right)\\cdot \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =4 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 4 x \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 2 x \\\\  & =2 x \\left(2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f77562-ab80-5d3b-9c6e-26b1a20e25e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526398} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5c61df-ca34-524f-b466-27fda668c5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526403} {:answer/id #uuid "85d35099-80ad-5ed2-9592-eb45ffba1d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526427} {:answer/id #uuid "c25f1ab3-e50f-5128-9601-38ee4a8d808e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526445} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7e74ea-a631-5bae-a39e-f283a9e26b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d5c61df-ca34-524f-b466-27fda668c5c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 36 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526403} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e1b94ef-858f-59cb-8303-ece73f491650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dab73ae4-4bf3-5f01-8c7a-eff6d6a066f0" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- 3 x e^{4 y}$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=- 3 e^{4 y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 12 x e^{4 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =- 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =- 12 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}+\\left(- 12 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =- 36 x e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} - 3 e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}} \\\\  & =- 3 \\left(12 x \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)} + 1\\right) e^{4 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}]}
